---
// Connecting a device (ADR 0269): a command line or another program shows a code and sends the
// person here. They check it is theirs, name the token, say if it should ever expire, and approve
// or deny. Rendered by renderDeviceConnect.
---

<div class="stack" data-device-connect>
  <!-- Without a code in the address: type the one the device shows. -->
  <form class="card card-body stack" data-code-form hidden>
    <p>
      A device (the <code>lorenzo</code> command line, for one) shows a code like
      <strong>ABCD-EFGH</strong>. Type it here to connect the device to your account.
    </p>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Code from your device</span>
      <input
        class="text-input"
        type="text"
        autocomplete="off"
        autocapitalize="characters"
        spellcheck="false"
        placeholder="ABCD-EFGH"
        data-code
      />
    </label>
    <div class="row">
      <button type="submit">Continue</button>
      <span class="status-text" role="status" data-code-status hidden></span>
    </div>
  </form>

  <!-- With a valid code: what is asking, and the choices. -->
  <form class="card card-body stack" data-approve-form hidden>
    <p>
      <strong data-client></strong> is asking to act as you on Lorenzo, with a personal access
      token. Connect it only if you started this yourself, just now.
    </p>
    <p class="caption">
      Code <strong data-shown-code></strong>. It can do what you can do, except manage personal
      access tokens or delete your account. You can revoke it at any time under your profile.
    </p>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Name this token</span>
      <input class="text-input" type="text" maxlength="80" required data-name />
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span class="field-label">It stops working</span>
      <select class="text-input" data-expiry></select>
    </label>
    <div class="row">
      <button type="submit" data-approve>
        Connect this device
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" data-deny>
        Deny
      </button>
      <span class="status-text" role="status" data-status hidden></span>
    </div>
  </form>

  <p class="status-text" role="status" data-result hidden></p>
</div>
